# Every failing disjunct reports its own error, also when the disjuncts
# share their positions, as the enum members the JSON Schema decoder
# produces do.
# https://cuelang.org/issue/4477

# TODO: the error against "three" is dropped, and only the first enum
# member carries the schema position.
! exec cue vet data.json jsonschema: schema.json
cmp stderr expect

-- schema.json --
{"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "enum": [1, 2, "three"]}
-- data.json --
0
-- expect --
2 errors in empty disjunction:
conflicting values 1 and 0:
    ./data.json:1:1
    ./schema.json:1:62
conflicting values 2 and 0:
    ./data.json:1:1
